# ⚠️ THIS FILE DOES NOTHING. `wrangler pages deploy` does NOT honour it.
#
# Verified 2026-08-18: start_server.py was listed here and still served at
# https://norsk-b2-pro.pages.dev/start_server.py on a freshly created deployment.
# .gitignore does not protect you either — wrangler uploads a directory from the
# filesystem, not the git tree.
#
# This is how ANTHROPIC_API_KEY leaked: .dev.vars sat in the repo root, git-ignored
# but world-readable at /.dev.vars on both the production and staging sites.
#
# ── Resolved 2026-08-27 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The durable fix this file used to recommend is now in place:
# wrangler.toml sets `pages_build_output_dir = "public"`, so deploys publish only
# what is inside public/ — currently norsk_b2_pro.html, lesing-tekster.json,
# _redirects and _headers. Everything else in the repo, including CLAUDE.md,
# start_server.py, tests/ and any stray .dev.vars, is no longer reachable.
#
# Verified by serving the tree with a .dev.vars present: GET /.dev.vars returned
# 404 with an empty body, as did /CLAUDE.md, /start_server.py and /package.json,
# while /norsk_b2_pro.html served all 425 KB.
#
# Publishing is now opt-in. To make a file public, put it in public/ — that is the
# only mechanism. Adding names to this file still does nothing.
#
# The old advice — keep secrets out of this directory — is no longer load-bearing,
# but remains good hygiene. Local secrets live in ~/.config/norskb2/.dev.vars.
